      "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
      "severity": "Severe",
      "urgency": "Immediate",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 31 at 1:20PM HST until October 31 at 2:45PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "At 120 PM HST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain falling over the eastern slopes of Kauai with additional\nshowers moving into the leeward side of the island. Rain was falling\nat a rate of 1 to 3 inches per hour. In addition to the Hanalei\nRiver, a rapid rise was also observed along the South Fork of the\nWailua River. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly,\nespecially near the Hanalei Bridge on the Kuhio Highway and near the\nmouth of the Wailua River. Law enforcement has closed Kuhio Highway\nnear the Hanalei Bridge.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nThe entire island of Kauai.",
      "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
