  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 312254\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM HST Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands:\nA broad area of low pressure is forecast to develop well to the\nsoutheast of the Hawaiian Islands by early next week. Thereafter,\nenvironmental conditions appear generally favorable for gradual\ndevelopment of this system, and a tropical depression could form by\nthe end of next week as it moves westward to west-northwestward over\nthe Central Pacific basin.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Evans/Beven\nNNNN",
